 ## Overview
-Automated Classification Widget Placement is an interaction technique that positions and sizes classification widgets in the transfer-function domain based on data probe feedback and reprojected voxel distributions [S1, book][S2]. It reduces the difficulty of manually creating effective higher-dimensional transfer functions by tying widget geometry to the statistical distribution of data at a specific probe location [S1, book][S2].
